  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2023</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2022</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1999</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2022</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is divisible by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math></p><p>Now we know that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;divides&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8704;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8469;</mi></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2023</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1999</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;divides&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2023</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2022</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1999</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2022</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>24</mn></math>&nbsp;divides&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2023</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2022</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1999</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2002</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;will divide&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2023</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2022</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1999</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2002</mn></msup></math></p><p>As&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;divides&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is correct</p><p>Now solving,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>13</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>13</mn></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn></math>&nbsp;is divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>144</mn></math>&nbsp;for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8469;</mi></math></p><p>So using binomial theorem in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>12</mn><msup><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mn>12</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><msup><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mn>12</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>13</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>12</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#955;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>145</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>144</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></math>&nbsp;which is&nbsp;not divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>144</mn></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is incorrect</p></blockquote>"
  }
